  "lineage": "Art and regional music of Afghanistan centered on the Kharabat quarter of Kabul, where Hindustani musicians brought from India in the 1860s under Amir Sher Ali Khan established hereditary ustad lineages, later broadcast nationally by Radio Kabul from the 1940s through figures such as Ustad Sarahang, Ustad Rahim Bakhsh and Ustad Mohammad Omar, marked by the plucked rubab with sympathetic strings, tabla and zerbaghali accompaniment, raga-derived naghma-e-kashal instrumental forms, and ghazal singing in Dari and Pashto.",
